  "articleBody": "It's awesome to tackle home projects yourself, but for certain home modifications, especially those focused on accessibility, bringing in an expert can make all the difference. Here are some signs it's time to call in the pros: \n*   **Structural elements are involved:** If your project means moving walls, changing door openings significantly, or impacting your home's structure, you really need a skilled contractor to ensure safety and compliance. \n*   **Complex bathroom layouts:** Installing curbless showers, modifying plumbing for new vanity heights, or ensuring proper drainage for roll-in showers often requires specialized knowledge. \n*   **Ramp geometry is tricky:** Getting the slope and length of a ramp just right is crucial for safety and usability, and it's not always as simple as it looks. \n*   **Funding or compliance requirements:** If you're working with Medicaid, VA, or other third-party programs, there can be specific rules and paperwork that an experienced professional can navigate for you. \n*   **Precise clearance planning is needed:** Especially for power wheelchairs or specific mobility devices, every inch matters. An expert can ensure all clearances are met. When these situations come up, reaching out to HH Remodeling LLC can save you a lot of hassle and ensure your modifications are done right.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
